        "raw": "<p>I was giving the new heroes a test drive (iOS version), and had all four of them (KNYFE, Naturalist, Sentinels, Parse) playing against Omnitron in the Wagner Mars Base. &nbsp;Naturalist was in his Gazelle form, so I played Hyperactive Senses, the text of which states:<br />&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&quot;Reveal the top 2 cards of any 2 decks, &nbsp;Put them back on top of their decks in any order. &nbsp; [And if in Gazelle Form]: You may discard the top card of any 2 decks.&quot; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The game first gave me the option to select a deck from which to reveal cards (I selected Parse), then another deck from which to reveal cards (I selected the environment). &nbsp;The game revealed the top two cards on each deck, then allowed me to rearrange them, per the card text. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here&#39;s where the bug/possible rules interpretation comes into play. &nbsp;Reading the card, it says &quot;<span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">[And if in Gazelle Form]: You may discard the top card of any 2 decks.&quot; &nbsp;Going with the traditional interpretation of cards that say &quot;may,&quot; I took that to mean that I could discard the top card of (a) two different decks, (b) only one deck, or (c) no decks at all. &nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">I went with choice (b) -- I wanted to discard the top card of the environment deck, but no others. &nbsp;However, once I had discarded the top deck of the environment deck, the game forced me to discard another top card; it didn&#39;t give me an option to skip the second. &nbsp;Not only that, but it made me discard a card from a different deck, even though the card does not say &quot;....discard the top card of any 2 *DIFFERENT* decks,&quot; or &quot;discard the top card from one deck, then another deck.&quot; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Is this a bug, or a rules interpretation? &nbsp;Is the &quot;Gazelle Form&quot; choice on the card an either/or -- either you discard two cards or none at all? &nbsp;If so, is that on purpose, or is it something that maybe/could/should be tweaked in a future edit?</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
